The objectionable section of SB 652 is also known as
the Gorton-Exon Amendment.  It is a revised version
of SB314.  The G-E Amendment no longer holds online
providers responsible for transmitted messages, but
does provide 2 years in the federal slammer for anyone
originating an "indecent", "filthy", "lewd" OR "obscene"
message of any kind, e.g., Usenet posting, E-MAIL, 
Web page, anonymous ftp offering....

IT IS TIME to contact your Senators and urge them to
oppose this!  Some talking points:  

--Business is increasingly dependent on e-mail, or
at least fond of it.  Business will NOT appreciate
anything which makes e-mail less private.  Giving
the feds the job of punishing "indecent" e-mail has
to make e-mail less private.

--Republicans are supposed to be decreasing regulation,
not increasing it.

--It is UNAMERICAN to be afraid of free speech, ditto
new technology.  The Gorton-Exon Amendment seems
inspired by fear and/or ignorance of both.

--It is no more constitutional to outlaw "indecent"
netspeech than "indecent" phone calls between consenting
parties or "indecent" snailmail.  Broadcast TV/radio
regulation is based on a completely different technical
situation (the feds are in the business, regrettably
one could say, of deciding who is "worthy" of 
access to limited broadcast frequencies).

--The bill is unnecessary, massive overkill for the
problem of parents not supervising kids' net access.
As for offensive e-mail, that can be dealt with as
harrassment, where appropriate, without the overall
censorship G-E would impose.

Please get on this, folks!

